/T (When are parallel arrays still better? When a program works on only one field for all patients, for example finding the average age. The ages are stored together in memory, so scanning is fast and no padding is wasted. Parallel arrays are also good when a field is added only for a few operations.)
/E (When are parallel arrays still better? When a program works on only one field for all patients, for example finding the average age. The ages are stored together in memory, so scanning is fast and no padding is wasted. Parallel arrays are also good when a field is added only for a few operations.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
