<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 133 0 R
/T (If the address and date were written directly inside the parcel \(a flat structure\), the fields would have to be repeated: sender_city, sender_pincode, receiver_city, receiver_pincode, day, month, year. The access path becomes shorter \(p.receiver_pincode instead of p.receiver.pincode\), but the address type cannot be reused, so one function like print_address\(const struct address *a\) cannot work for both sender and receiver, and the date cannot be passed alone to a date function.)
/E (If the address and date were written directly inside the parcel \(a flat structure\), the fields would have to be repeated: sender_city, sender_pincode, receiver_city, receiver_pincode, day, month, year. The access path becomes shorter \(p.receiver_pincode instead of p.receiver.pincode\), but the address type cannot be reused, so one function like print_address\(const struct address *a\) cannot work for both sender and receiver, and the date cannot be passed alone to a date function.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [17]
>>
