<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 135 0 R
/T (The structure is not 4 + 4 + 4 + 8 = 20 bytes, because the union members share the same memory. The union takes only 8 bytes \(the biggest member\), not 4 + 4 + 8. So the structure is 4 \(tag\) + 8 \(union\) = 12 bytes.)
/E (The structure is not 4 + 4 + 4 + 8 = 20 bytes, because the union members share the same memory. The union takes only 8 bytes \(the biggest member\), not 4 + 4 + 8. So the structure is 4 \(tag\) + 8 \(union\) = 12 bytes.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [35]
>>
