/Title (In the structure design, all details of a patient stay together in one record. To sort by age we swap one whole structure, so a name can never be separated from its age. A patient can be passed to a function with one pointer instead of five values. New data, like a blood group, is added as one new member and the old code still works. Nested structures keep date and blood pressure clear, and the date can be compared easily. A count check stops overflow.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1764 0 R
>>
endobj
