1858 0 obj
<<
/Title (int next_token\(int *counter\) { return ++\(*counter\); } \(program t5d.c, output above\). Time: O\(1\) in every version, since each call does one increment. Space and lifetime: the counter is an ordinary variable in the caller \(4 bytes\), and it lives as long as the caller wants. The function itself has no hidden memory, so it is easy to test and has no global state. Two independent counters: very easy; just declare two variables \(veg, nonveg\) and pass the address of the one needed, with no change to the function at all. The only cost is that the caller must create and pass the counter.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1845 0 R
>>
endobj
