/Title (When the three calls were moved into one printf, this machine printed 1003 1002 1001 \(the arguments were evaluated from right to left\), instead of 1001 1002 1003. C does not specify the order in which function arguments are evaluated, so the compiler can choose any order. Separate statements \(int s1 = next_token\(\), s2 = ..., s3 = ...\) give a fixed order, so they should be used when the order matters.)
/Dest [24 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1857 0 R
