<<
/Title (Design A \(structure\): struct packet_struct { float celsius; int percent; char status[8]; } holds all three values at the same time. Design B \(tagged union\): struct reading { enum kind type; union { float celsius; int percent; char status[8]; } value; }. A packet carries exactly one kind of value, so the union shares one memory area, and the tag \(type\) tells which member is valid. Design B suits the station, because it has very little memory and stores thousands of packets: it saves 4 bytes in every packet.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1907 0 R
>>
endobj
