<<
/Title (The output above shows two different addresses: the account inside addInterest\(\) is stored at a different address \(inside the function's own stack frame\) than list[0] in main\(\). So the function worked on a copy. The balances printed from main\(\) are still 5000, 12000 and 800. In the repaired program the function prints the same address as list[0] for the first account, so it works on the original.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1984 0 R
>>
