2008 0 obj
<<
/Title (Defect 1 \(balances do not change\): addInterest\(struct account a, ...\) receives the structure by value. C makes a copy of list[i], the interest is added to the copy, and the copy is thrown away when the function ends. The original in main\(\) is never touched.)
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1998 0 R
/Next 2009 0 R
>>
endobj
2009 0 obj
<<
/Title (Defect 2 \(does not compile\): p is a pointer \(struct account *p = list\), but the program uses p.number and p.balance. The dot operator works only on a structure variable. For a pointer the arrow operator is needed \(p->number, p->balance\). The compiler reported: "'p' is a pointer; did you mean to use '->'?")
/Dest [20 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1998 0 R
/Prev 2008 0 R
>>
endobj
