2012 0 obj
<<
/Title (Pass by value: the function gets a copy, so changes are lost. Pass by pointer: the function gets the address of the original, so changes are kept. The arrow operator \(a->balance\) is the short form of \(*a\).balance.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2003 0 R
/Next 2013 0 R
>>
endobj
2013 0 obj
<<
/Title (The dot operator is used with a structure variable, and the arrow operator with a pointer to a structure. Using the wrong one is a compile-time error.)
/Dest [19 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2003 0 R
/Prev 2012 0 R
>>
endobj
